      "value": "@{608c3912f10152388b7ad184|full_name}  @{5f04ccd86dd7706aba03bbdf|full_name}  I've looked at your uploaded avatars, and it appears your tangent data is messed up. See attached screenshots. Toon Standard uses tangent data to calculate lighting, including specular, which leads to this result. Usually tangents should be smooth like your vertex normals.\n\nI've adjusted the shader to apply the reflectance value to fresnel regardless, which did appear a bit incorrect, but the root issue comes from this.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
