  "details": "Several of my avatars seem to not play nicely with the new Toon Standard shader, specifically the reflectance. Even when Gloss and Metallic are set to 0, as long as there's any reflectance value, areas on meshes with heavy amounts of custom split vertex normal data reflect things far too intensely. This was tested and reproducable with several models that use custom split vertex normals for eye shading.\n\nHere is an avatar blueprint with the issue: https://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_49fd3f99-59d4-47d0-be65-5f757729908d",
